// The version being replaced by edit_diverges_both_ways.dw. See that file for what the pair is
// for.
//
// Approvals are allowed unconditionally and trades are not allowed at all -- there is no permit
// for Trade, so it is denied by default. That second fact is what makes the pair discriminating:
// no trade ever completes under this policy, so no `Trade::response` is ever recorded, so the
// forbid in the new file never arms along any history this policy can produce.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Approve",
    resource
);
